WEBVTT

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:14.806
This will only lead to trouble.
Forget about her and go home.

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:16.975
Huh?

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:21.563
If you don't, you'll be trapped
here the next time you visit.

00:00:27.611 --> 00:00:29.905
What was that?

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:32.866
The Space-Time Man,

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:36.245
a middle-aged man people encounter
when suddenly finding themselves

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:38.372
in a strange world with no one else around.

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:43.001
He's part of the "wandered into
another world" genre of horror stories.

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:46.672
It's said he's a member of
a surveillance organization

00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:49.132
that guards against
intrusions into the Otherside

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:53.303
and tries to send back anyone who wanders in.

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:58.767
But why a middle-aged man?
Why not something cuter?

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:51.737
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:32.194
Your order's ready.

00:02:32.194 --> 00:02:37.991
Taco rice, chocolate and
sour cherry cake, and strawberry tarts.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.952
Please enjoy.

00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:47.000
So, what next?

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.629
Listen, we're gonna end up
dead one of these days.

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:52.130
What?

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:58.095
It's been one brush with death
after another and still no sign of Satsuki.

00:02:58.095 --> 00:03:03.600
But... Satsuki could be in danger as we speak.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.186
She disappeared three months ago.

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:09.773
Three months without a word
from someone in that world...

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:12.192
Satsuki is already...

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.530
She's alive.

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:22.035
I know Satsuki's still alive.

00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:28.584
She's someone special to me,
so I need your help.

00:03:28.584 --> 00:03:34.715
But... you're asking me to risk my life
for someone I've never even met.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.889
I see.

00:03:43.265 --> 00:03:44.933
Sorry.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.439
I'll take it from here. Thanks.

00:03:50.439 --> 00:03:52.441
Hey, wait!

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.196
Jeez, that's not what I meant.

00:03:57.196 --> 00:04:01.241
I just wanted to say we
should stop because I'm scared.

00:04:02.951 --> 00:04:05.996
So? Why are you here?

00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:11.251
I tried to patch things up after that,
but when I went to her place...

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:16.632
I knew something was wrong
when I opened the door.

00:04:16.632 --> 00:04:19.009
The Space-Time Man kept getting mad at me.

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:21.428
The <i>what </i>man?

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.141
And I'm getting scary texts.

00:04:26.141 --> 00:04:31.522
I'm really worried now that I know
Toriko went to the Otherside alone.

00:04:31.522 --> 00:04:34.316
I was hoping you'd come help me find her.

00:04:34.316 --> 00:04:37.069
No. It's too much trouble.

00:04:37.069 --> 00:04:42.616
Besides, you look all fired up.
So stop bothering me and just go.

00:04:42.616 --> 00:04:44.952
Aren't you worried about Toriko?

00:04:44.952 --> 00:04:46.870
I'm not cut out for fieldwork.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.873
I can't handle all that running
and jumping like you guys.

00:04:49.873 --> 00:04:51.500
But...

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.919
Let me see that again.

00:04:56.922 --> 00:05:01.468
That face would crack a mirror. Hm? What's this?

00:05:01.468 --> 00:05:05.055
Hm? Where'd that photo come from?

00:05:05.055 --> 00:05:11.854
It was before the ugly face.
It was taken on May 14th.

00:05:11.854 --> 00:05:15.482
That was the day I met Toriko.

00:05:15.482 --> 00:05:18.277
I wonder who that woman is.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.446
Satsuki Uruma.

00:05:21.446 --> 00:05:22.364
Huh?

00:05:22.364 --> 00:05:25.200
That's who Toriko's looking for.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.661
That's her?

00:05:27.661 --> 00:05:29.371
I don't like this.

00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:34.626
Clusters of illogical phenomena
that seem to mean something.

00:05:34.626 --> 00:05:40.007
But is this a threat or
a revelation? I just can't tell.

00:05:40.007 --> 00:05:42.759
Like that time with Satsuki.

00:05:46.555 --> 00:05:51.852
Pardon me. I wanted to speak
to you about your neighbor.

00:05:51.852 --> 00:05:53.520
Might I have a word?

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.105
Huh?

00:05:55.105 --> 00:05:57.441
Something's not right.

00:05:57.441 --> 00:05:57.649
--They remind me of the Space-Time Man!

00:05:57.649 --> 00:06:03.447
--Pardon me.
--They remind me of the Space-Time Man!

00:06:03.447 --> 00:06:05.616
--Is anyone home?
--They remind me of the Space-Time Man!

00:06:09.286 --> 00:06:10.829
Whoa, what is that?

00:06:10.829 --> 00:06:11.955
Is anyone home?!

00:06:11.955 --> 00:06:16.293
It's an M870, your garden
variety 12-gauge shotgun.

00:06:16.293 --> 00:06:18.795
Garden variety?

00:06:18.795 --> 00:06:19.838
Pardon me!

00:06:19.838 --> 00:06:22.424
Enough, already! I'll shoot!

00:06:24.635 --> 00:06:25.636
Open it.

00:06:25.636 --> 00:06:27.346
Who, me?

00:06:27.346 --> 00:06:30.098
I won't get any work done
till we get rid of them!

00:06:33.936 --> 00:06:38.232
So far, the wiggle-waggles and
Lady Hasshaku on the Otherside

00:06:38.232 --> 00:06:41.568
have been just like the
urban legends people tell.

00:06:41.568 --> 00:06:45.405
Is that because they exert
some sort of influence on this side?

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:52.204
Then why stop short like this?
Or was ding-dong-ditch what they--

00:07:10.764 --> 00:07:13.016
The Otherside.

00:07:16.645 --> 00:07:20.732
What the actual hell?! Look what I'm wearing!
Are you trying to kill me?!

00:07:21.859 --> 00:07:25.112
As long as we're here, let's go find Toriko.

00:07:25.112 --> 00:07:29.658
Sorawo, you really do
have nice written all over you.

00:07:29.658 --> 00:07:32.077
Huh?

00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:37.583
Jeez, fine. I'll go.
That's what you want, isn't it?

00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:40.836
Yay!

00:07:40.836 --> 00:07:43.088
This sucks.

00:08:04.026 --> 00:08:05.527
Are you all right?

00:08:05.527 --> 00:08:07.529
Listen, Sorawo.

00:08:07.529 --> 00:08:08.947
What?

00:08:08.947 --> 00:08:13.243
Some people can handle haunted houses.
Others freeze in fear.

00:08:13.243 --> 00:08:15.704
Oh, I've never actually been to one.

00:08:15.704 --> 00:08:17.122
Me, either.

00:08:17.122 --> 00:08:18.081
Hm?

00:08:18.081 --> 00:08:21.293
Well, it could be a horror
movie or anything, really.

00:08:21.293 --> 00:08:24.129
The point is people respond to fear differently.

00:08:24.129 --> 00:08:28.634
The serotonin transporter gene
determines whether you're easily scared.

00:08:28.634 --> 00:08:34.640
A long gene activation sequence means
your nerve cells will produce more serotonin,

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.019
and you'll tend to be less anxious.
In short, you're harder to scare.

00:08:39.019 --> 00:08:40.646
Okay...

00:08:40.646 --> 00:08:43.148
My gene for that is short.

00:08:43.148 --> 00:08:45.984
Oh, so you're a total scaredy-cat!

00:08:48.362 --> 00:08:54.326
Damn right, I'm scared! Scared to death!
I never wanted to come here again.

00:08:54.326 --> 00:08:56.703
I'm basically useless here,
so keep your eyes peeled!

00:08:56.703 --> 00:08:59.289
You've got a shotgun. You'll be fine.

00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:02.084
This puppy finds its mark
even with my eyes shut.

00:09:02.084 --> 00:09:03.126
What?

00:09:03.126 --> 00:09:05.921
So I might end up accidently shooting you.

00:09:05.921 --> 00:09:07.756
How about you go first?!

00:09:07.756 --> 00:09:09.550
No can do.

00:09:11.718 --> 00:09:14.680
You sure have strong legs.

00:09:17.432 --> 00:09:20.936
Maybe it was all the
walking I did in high school.

00:09:20.936 --> 00:09:23.272
I'd go explore ruins and stuff alone.

00:09:23.272 --> 00:09:25.774
That's a dangerous hobby.

00:09:25.774 --> 00:09:28.026
Ⅰ was a bit reckless back then.

00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:29.152
How come?

00:09:29.152 --> 00:09:31.488
It's not a big deal.

00:09:31.488 --> 00:09:33.031
Go on.

00:09:33.031 --> 00:09:39.788
My mom died young, and my dad
and grandma joined this weird cult.

00:09:39.788 --> 00:09:42.374
After that, I had nowhere to go.

00:09:42.374 --> 00:09:45.002
They tried to abduct me on
the way home from school

00:09:45.002 --> 00:09:47.629
and burn down the manga
café where I was crashing.

00:09:47.629 --> 00:09:50.048
So I started camping out in ruins.

00:09:50.048 --> 00:09:55.262
Then one night, I dreamt that this
really soft red person was hugging me.

00:09:55.262 --> 00:09:57.514
When they asked, "You don't need them?"

00:09:57.514 --> 00:10:02.644
I said that I didn't. After that, I went back
home with some kerosene and waited.

00:10:02.644 --> 00:10:03.979
Kerosene?

00:10:03.979 --> 00:10:07.441
But after waiting for days,
no one ever came home.

00:10:07.441 --> 00:10:09.568
Just when I started feeling relieved,

00:10:09.568 --> 00:10:13.280
I got a call about their bodies
being found in the mountains.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.200
They'd been killed by gas
that settled in a hollow.

00:10:17.284 --> 00:10:18.785
I was now on my own.

00:10:18.785 --> 00:10:21.413
I went to college on a student loan,

00:10:21.413 --> 00:10:25.083
but I had no inheritance, so it felt
like I'd never be able to repay it.

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:29.838
Just when I ran out of ideas,
that's when I met Toriko.

00:10:29.838 --> 00:10:34.635
Sorry. I didn't mean to bore you.
It's no big deal.

00:10:34.635 --> 00:10:37.054
You really believe that?

00:10:37.054 --> 00:10:40.724
Is something wrong? I thought
my story is a rather common one.

00:10:40.724 --> 00:10:45.938
Not even. You've had some serious bad luck, too.

00:10:45.938 --> 00:10:49.399
Well, at least now I know why
you're tougher than you look.

00:10:49.399 --> 00:10:51.193
Could've fooled me, though.

00:10:51.193 --> 00:10:54.530
You don't have a strong presence like Toriko.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:57.366
Compared to Toriko, I'm...

00:10:57.366 --> 00:10:59.952
Why do you suppose she's like that?

00:10:59.952 --> 00:11:02.746
She was born in Canada.
Her parents were in the military.

00:11:02.746 --> 00:11:05.499
They taught her lots of stuff from a young age.

00:11:05.499 --> 00:11:08.293
Oh, that's why she's good with guns.

00:11:08.293 --> 00:11:13.006
She's not easily scared and is true to Satsuki.

00:11:13.006 --> 00:11:15.717
It's like she was born to go to the Otherside.

00:11:15.717 --> 00:11:18.220
Are her parents still in Canada?

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:20.430
I heard they passed away.

00:11:25.811 --> 00:11:27.688
It's freezing.

00:11:27.688 --> 00:11:31.275
I don't have any extra clothes,
but I could wrap my arms around you.

00:11:31.275 --> 00:11:32.401
Huh?

00:11:32.401 --> 00:11:34.111
I didn't mean anything by that.

00:11:34.111 --> 00:11:35.237
Stop!

00:11:35.237 --> 00:11:39.199
Either say what you mean
or don't say anything at all!

00:11:39.199 --> 00:11:41.535
O-Okay...

00:11:44.746 --> 00:11:48.125
Sorawo, do you have a lighter or something?

00:11:51.587 --> 00:11:54.423
I'm gonna climb up and have a look.

00:12:06.977 --> 00:12:10.939
Just relax. Pretend it's nothing,
just like you did before.

00:12:10.939 --> 00:12:14.484
Oh, but I was with Toriko.

00:12:14.484 --> 00:12:18.155
Look how scared I am just 'cause she's not here.

00:12:18.155 --> 00:12:22.576
We have similar circumstances,
but she's nothing like me.

00:12:22.576 --> 00:12:24.995
She has something I don't.

00:12:24.995 --> 00:12:28.415
But something else is
lacking more than it is with me.

00:12:28.415 --> 00:12:34.671
She came out of nowhere and really
did a number on me before disappearing.

00:12:34.671 --> 00:12:39.426
I don't need you. I can do this myself.

00:12:39.426 --> 00:12:41.094
So...

00:12:42.179 --> 00:12:45.849
Hurry up and come back, Toriko!

00:12:58.946 --> 00:13:00.614
Toriko!

00:13:04.368 --> 00:13:06.745
Can't she hear me?

00:13:14.086 --> 00:13:16.547
Kozakura...

00:13:16.547 --> 00:13:19.174
She was so scared and yet...

00:13:32.229 --> 00:13:34.731
It's all one big glitch?

00:13:34.731 --> 00:13:40.696
Normally, I wouldn't go anywhere
near there, but I saw Toriko.

00:13:44.491 --> 00:13:46.451
Hey!

00:13:46.451 --> 00:13:50.956
Why have you returned?
I told you you'll be trapped here.

00:14:13.395 --> 00:14:18.817
No way. Is this what happened
to the people who lived here?

00:14:19.943 --> 00:14:23.280
--Sorawo! Hey, are you listening to me?!
What's wrong with you, Sorawo?!

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:25.240
--Is that...?
--Sorawo! Hey, are you listening to me?!
What's wrong with you, Sorawo?!

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:26.783
--Is that...?
--Sorawo! I'm talking to you!
I'm right here, you idiot!

00:14:26.783 --> 00:14:30.495
--Sorawo! I'm talking to you!
I'm right here, you idiot!

00:14:30.495 --> 00:14:32.372
Kozakura?

00:14:33.457 --> 00:14:35.501
I finally got through to you.

00:14:35.501 --> 00:14:38.003
I kept calling you,
but you wouldn't look this way.

00:14:38.003 --> 00:14:42.049
Sorry. I saw these weird
plants, but they're gone.

00:14:44.343 --> 00:14:46.929
What are you doing here?

00:14:46.929 --> 00:14:48.514
Satsuki called to me.

00:14:48.514 --> 00:14:49.932
What?

00:14:49.932 --> 00:14:53.310
I remember I started walking,
thinking I better check it out.

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:56.355
The next thing I knew,
I was in the middle of this town.

00:14:56.355 --> 00:14:58.106
Did you see Toriko?

00:14:58.106 --> 00:14:59.107
No.

00:14:59.107 --> 00:15:04.696
Oh, I see. Kozakura, you should
head back now. It'll be dark soon.

00:15:04.696 --> 00:15:06.448
Head back where?

00:15:06.448 --> 00:15:09.493
There's an elevator on
the building's roof. Use it to--

00:15:09.493 --> 00:15:12.371
Are you insane?!
Like I could make it back myself!

00:15:12.371 --> 00:15:16.667
It's right there if you run. Here.

00:15:16.667 --> 00:15:17.793
I'm going, too.

00:15:17.793 --> 00:15:19.795
What?

00:15:19.795 --> 00:15:24.967
I want to see Satsuki... if she's still alive.

00:15:29.221 --> 00:15:32.307
You mentioned something about plants?

00:15:32.307 --> 00:15:36.728
You looked like a plant just a moment ago,
but that gave me an idea.

00:15:36.728 --> 00:15:41.608
My eye stripped away the
Otherside's veil of illusion many times.

00:15:41.608 --> 00:15:45.612
But I've never used this ability on a glitch.

00:15:45.612 --> 00:15:48.407
That man suddenly wasn't a man anymore.

00:15:48.407 --> 00:15:50.909
So if this town isn't really a town,

00:15:50.909 --> 00:15:55.581
I should be able to spot Toriko
by seeing the glitch's true nature.

00:15:55.581 --> 00:15:57.541
There's no other way?

00:15:57.541 --> 00:15:59.835
I'll come back for you.

00:15:59.835 --> 00:16:03.755
I guess I have no choice. I believe in you.

00:16:03.755 --> 00:16:06.425
Okay, I'll be back.

00:16:20.689 --> 00:16:22.816
That's...

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:32.159
Toriko's apartment building.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:41.460
W-Wait!

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.796
It's creepy seeing someone
who looks just like you.

00:16:44.796 --> 00:16:46.465
But...

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:03.148
Toriko!

00:17:07.694 --> 00:17:10.197
Sorawo. You came for me.

00:17:10.197 --> 00:17:13.700
Of course, I did!
I was looking for you like crazy!

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:17.454
Oh... I didn't think you'd come.

00:17:17.454 --> 00:17:20.290
What're you talking about? C'mon, let's go.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:22.292
Sorry. I can't leave.

00:17:22.292 --> 00:17:23.585
What?

00:17:25.504 --> 00:17:27.631
I found her.

00:17:31.885 --> 00:17:34.137
Satsuki Uruma.

00:17:34.137 --> 00:17:38.600
Wait, no. That isn't...

00:17:41.603 --> 00:17:45.858
Satsuki's my special someone.

00:17:45.858 --> 00:17:52.114
She taught me so much
and took me to the Otherside.

00:17:52.114 --> 00:17:57.494
She said there was still so
much more she would teach me, but...

00:17:57.494 --> 00:17:58.954
No!

00:17:58.954 --> 00:18:02.583
I finally found her. I knew she was still alive.

00:18:02.583 --> 00:18:05.127
I have to go. I must join Satsuki.

00:18:05.127 --> 00:18:07.254
No, don't! Toriko!

00:18:07.254 --> 00:18:11.091
That... That isn't her!

00:18:18.599 --> 00:18:20.434
Toriko!

00:18:20.434 --> 00:18:25.022
Sorawo, now I finally understand.

00:18:25.022 --> 00:18:30.402
I know why Satsuki disappeared
and why I was called here.

00:18:30.402 --> 00:18:32.863
There's something beyond there.

00:18:32.863 --> 00:18:40.537
We really <i>should </i>be scared,
so scared that it drives us insane.

00:18:40.537 --> 00:18:47.419
All creatures experience fear, but only
humans willingly imagine and use it.

00:18:47.419 --> 00:18:52.341
That's why they use fear
to gain access to our minds.

00:18:52.341 --> 00:18:56.136
They are so alien to us,
so utterly incomprehensible

00:18:56.136 --> 00:19:01.225
that fear is the only channel
through which contact is possible.

00:19:01.225 --> 00:19:04.811
Fear is their means of interaction.
That is their objective.

00:19:04.811 --> 00:19:07.356
Sorawo, I figured it all out.

00:19:07.356 --> 00:19:09.274
No! Don't!

00:19:10.776 --> 00:19:13.946
Stop it. I'm going alone.

00:19:13.946 --> 00:19:16.490
No way! I'm not letting you go!

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:19.660
I mean, how dare you after what you did to me?!

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:23.914
I won't let them take you.
I don't care who or what they are!

00:19:23.914 --> 00:19:26.792
I'll blow you away! You hear me?!

00:19:33.507 --> 00:19:36.051
Satsuki.

00:20:08.333 --> 00:20:12.379
Huh? That's not Satsuki!

00:20:12.379 --> 00:20:16.216
What's happening?! I feel like I'm going insane!

00:20:16.216 --> 00:20:21.013
Just take it easy. It'll pass... probably.

00:20:27.436 --> 00:20:31.315
Wait. I think we'll be all right.

00:20:31.315 --> 00:20:35.861
Uh, Sorawo? What exactly was I trying to do?

00:20:35.861 --> 00:20:39.072
That monster was trying to
lure you to God knows where.

00:20:39.072 --> 00:20:40.866
Umm...

00:20:40.866 --> 00:20:43.035
I'm really sorry.

00:20:43.035 --> 00:20:46.038
I'll never forgive you, but no worries.

00:20:46.038 --> 00:20:47.581
But I'll never forgive you.

00:20:47.581 --> 00:20:49.249
Which is it?!

00:20:49.249 --> 00:20:52.753
FYI, it's partly your fault, too.

00:20:52.753 --> 00:20:53.587
Huh?

00:20:53.587 --> 00:20:56.798
You said you won't go with me,
and I'm not your friend anymore.

00:20:56.798 --> 00:20:58.884
That was a total shock!

00:20:58.884 --> 00:21:00.594
Hey, I never said that!

00:21:00.594 --> 00:21:02.137
It sure sounded like it!

00:21:02.137 --> 00:21:05.557
You can make up for it by
figuring out how to get out of here.

00:21:05.557 --> 00:21:09.269
T-Talk about high maintenance.

00:21:09.269 --> 00:21:11.063
Come on.

00:21:17.152 --> 00:21:18.403
What now?

00:21:18.403 --> 00:21:20.531
Grab on to whatever over there.

00:21:20.531 --> 00:21:22.407
Okay.

00:21:29.331 --> 00:21:31.834
By the way, I forgot tell you...

00:21:31.834 --> 00:21:33.043
Hm?

00:21:33.043 --> 00:21:35.838
Thanks for coming.

00:21:37.673 --> 00:21:41.426
So, when are we doing this again?

00:21:41.426 --> 00:21:42.886
Huh?

00:21:42.886 --> 00:21:46.431
Seriously?!

00:21:51.395 --> 00:21:55.357
Sorawo, where are you?

00:21:57.776 --> 00:21:58.026
What's taking so long?

00:21:58.026 --> 00:22:01.613
"Space, Time, and a Middle-Aged Man"
What's taking so long?

00:22:01.613 --> 00:22:01.989
"Space, Time, and a Middle-Aged Man"

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:35.082
We'll leave it at that.
Do you understand, you two?

00:23:35.082 --> 00:23:36.291
Yes, sorry.

00:23:36.291 --> 00:23:38.377
No more deserting you.

00:23:38.377 --> 00:23:39.628
She really chewed us out.

00:23:39.628 --> 00:23:42.339
Poor Kozakura. Lecturing people
is hard when you're a shut-in.

00:23:42.339 --> 00:23:47.072
You're the last person I want
to hear that from, Sorawo.
